---
source: crates/wolf_mem/tests/mem_diagnostics.rs
expression: render_mem(&src)
---
error[E1001]: `m[true]` is used here after its value moved away
  --> mem:///main.lu:12:13
   |
 8 |     var v = m[k] else List[int]()
   |             ---- `m[k]` moved here
...
12 |     let w = m[true] else List[int]()
   |             ^^^^^^^ used after the move
   |
   = note: `m[true]` may reach the moved `m[k]`: an index that is not a literal is one place with
     every other index of its container [mem.model.place.elem]. Distinct literal indices stay
     usable.
   = note: re-initializing the place (assigning to it) also makes it usable again.
help: to keep the original, copy it at the move
   |
 8 |     var v = copy m[k] else List[int]()
   |
